      "text": "To find the product of the base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) and then determine the base seven sum of the digits, we first convert these base seven numbers to base ten.\n\nStarting with \\(24_7\\):\n\\[\n24_7 = 2 \\times 7^1 + 4 \\times 7^0 = 2 \\times 7 + 4 \\times 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\n\\]\n\nNext, for \\(30_7\\):\n\\[\n30_7 = 3 \\times 7^1 + 0 \\times 7^0 = 3 \\times 7 + 0 \\times 1 = 21_{10}\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the product in base ten:\n\\[\n18 \\times 21 = 378_{10}\n\\]\n\nNext, we convert \\(378_{10}\\) back to base seven. We do this by finding out how many complete powers of 7 fit into 378:\n\\[\n378 \\div 7 = 54 \\text{ with no remainder} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 378 = 54 \\times 7^1\n\\]\nSince 54 is also divisible by 7:\n\\[\n54 \\div 7 = 7 \\text{ with a remainder of} 5 \\Rightarrow 54 = 7 \\times 7^1 + 5 \\Rightarrow 54 = 49 + 5\n\\]\nContinuing the process:\n\\[\n49 \\div 7 = 7 \\text{ with no remainder} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 49 = 7 \\times 7^1\n\\]\nSo far, we have:\n\\[\n54 = 7 \\times 7^1 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\n49 = 7 \\times 7^0 = 7^1\n\\]\n\nCombining these results:\n\\[\n378 = 54 \\times 7^1 + 49 \\times 7^0 = (7^1 \\times 7 + 7^1 \\times 7 + 49) = 7 \\times (49 + 7\\cdot14 + 49) = 7 \\times (49 + 98 + 49) = 7 \\times 196 = 1378_{7} = 1 \\times 7^3 + 3 \\times 7^2 + 7 \\times 7^1 + 1 \\times 7^0 = 1 \\times 343 + 3 \\times 49 + 7 \\times 7 + 1 = 343 + 147 + 49 + 1 = 540_{10}\n\\]\n\nThe digits of the product in base seven are \\(1, 1, 1, 0,\\) and \\(1\\). The sum of these digits is:\n\\[\n1 + 1 + 1 + 0 + 1 = 4\n\\]\n\nSo the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
